hey what's up guys and welcome to a live  introduction to PvP in blood-borne I  usually script my content I don't  usually narrate live so I'm not that  used to it but I figured I want to  describe what I'm doing in real time and  I know that'll make it harder for me to  PvP but I do feel like it'll be worth it  so here's our first opponent the first  thing you're going to notice about PvP  in this game is that healing is  incredibly easy to pull off as a result  we're going to want to shoot him with  our pistol while he's at range and  trying to heal and just generally try to  stay as close to him as possible so here  we go he's buffed his weapon so I should  do that too  so right now he should be looking to  heal and you can tell so I'm going to  make sure he doesn't get the chance to  do that so there you go  but Bourne PvP so that's enough live  commentary I really want to tell you  everything I've learned about the PvP  thus far and also tell you about my  first impressions of it so to start you  might be wondering how invading works as  soon as you have ten insight you'll be  able to by the sinister resonant Bell  from the insight vendor in the hunters  dream  whenever you ring this bell in the  overworld it's going to attempt to form  a connection with a bell maiden in  somebody else's world so your next  question is what is a bell Maiden well  basically she is the link between you  and another players world your Bell  interacts with the Bell that she's  ringing and you can only invade a player  who has her in their world as far as I  know there are two ways to make her  appear the first most common way is by  ringing the beckoning Bell to invite  helpers into your world whenever you  summon help using the beckoning Bell you  consume one inside point and also summon  a Bell Maiden into your world for  example this is her location in all the  Arnim and a part of this is finding out  where she is when she spawns because the  Bell maiden as I mentioned before will  draw invaders meaning that whenever you  initiate co-op you're pretty much  begging for invaders to come and get you  so your objective when you initiate  co-op is to find this spell maiden and  killer if you like and hopefully you do  this before you get invaded by someone  the second way to summon her is more or  less a confirmed rumor at this point  there are reports that whenever you ring  the sinister resonant Bell to invade  somebody else's world there is a chance  that you can summon a bell maiden in  your own world so basically whenever you  ring the bell to invade it also might  make you open to invasions from other  people and this is a really clever thing  because if you want to invade someone  then you're perfectly okay with someone  invading you as well right and if this  happens it's better because it's  to be one-on-one it's going to be a  jewel and you both want to be VP moving  on in some areas the bell maiden will be  there from the very beginning no matter  what for example the one in nightmares  frontier is always here regardless of  whether you summon help or not and that  is why I've been here all day so I  suppose you could call this a designated  PvP area because invaders will find it  very easy to find your world it's the  best place to try and invade if you want  one-on-one fights instead of fighting  ganks banks and fighting people who are  engaging in co-op I've been enjoying  this so much just fighting people in  nightmares frontier having so much fun I  mean I'm sure you can see from the clips  how cool the PvP looks in this game it's  so different and fast-paced and hectic  and frantic I loved it and I found that  I never run out of insight either so  when you ring the bell to invade people  it doesn't use up the insight point when  you invade them and die that's when you  lose the insight point but if you invade  them and succeed you gain an insight  point so think about it this means that  if you have a better than 50% win ratio  then you can indefinitely invade people  which is really awesome I've just been  spending all my insight points that I've  been getting on fire paper because I  love this flaming great sword how good  does it look the last thing I want to  say about the bell maiden is that as it  stands I don't think there is a way to  invade someone who doesn't have a bell  maiden in their world so you're going to  either be killing people in coop or  fighting people who are in the PvP zones  of the game and once you've killed the  boss of the level I don't think you can  summon or get invaded anymore so moving  on to what I think about the PvP in  regards to the moment-by-moment gameplay  let me show you this clip where I in  vade two players in coop earlier I  mentioned that it can be super difficult  to kill people who are dead set on  healing and co-op is an enhanced version  of this problem each of them could  potentially have 20 blood vials which  can make for some seriously drawn-out  fights this fight lasted 20 minutes and  I've heard about people having fights  that lasted an hour or more the combat  of blood-borne is incredibly fun  fast-paced don't get me wrong but you  should expect some seriously long fights  in the early game at least and that's a  point I have to make I'm only halfway  through the game and these are my first  impressions I think it's fair to be  worried about healing or other concerns  about the PvP but it's definitely way  too early to make judgments because who  really knows what the late-game is going  to bring and the fights right now  they're not that bad just because  they're drawn-out doesn't mean they're  unfair if you aren't play your opponent  that just means he'll go through his  blood vials faster than you will so you  can still outplay him healing isn't  unfair in that regard all it does is  draw the fights out a lot and the  interesting thing about that is since  I'm invading halfway through the game I  haven't finished the game the guy I'm  invading hasn't finished the game and he  wants his blood vials he doesn't want to  waste them in PvP so while it does draw  out the fight  there are definitely drawbacks to using  them and the length of the fight itself  depends on how cowardly the people you  fight in co-op are so many people I  fought were chickens like look at these  two guys these two guys barely  progressed through the level because  they knew I was waiting for them behind  enemies and they knew that was the only  way I would be able to kill them if they  agro the enemies and you'll find this  happens often if someone needs help with  the level chances are they're probably  not that great of a player or a bit  cowardly in general that's just the way  it is so the best way to kill people in  co-op is to engage them while they're  fighting the enemies of the level and  once you do this the fight gets  incredibly fun and frantic enemies do a  fair bit of damage to other players more  than you will anyway and staggering them  while they fight a group of enemies can  make it seriously hard for the player to  sustain that much damage it's also the  only chance I've ever found myself  having to throw numbing mist at them  numbing mist is essentially the Lloyds  talisman of blood-borne they're stopping  opponents from healing you can see this  guy frantically trying to heal and  wondering what's wrong with his heal  button that was funny now in my  experience they're fairly easy to dodge  which is a huge problem because if the  enemy realizes you're about to throw  they'll be able to avoid it with ease I  mean look at all these throws where my  target moves a little bit and they still  miss there's one clip where he's like  half bent over and it goes over his head  it's ridiculous it should be way easier  to hit with these things I don't think  there's ever been a game where it's been  valid to throw these at the opponent and  that's a problem because you should have  the ability to stop healing for a short  amount of time or something like that  and so far I've found no way to buy  these from a merchant so you're limited  to the amount you find out in the world  but that again might change in the late  game so until we learn a little bit more  about late game pvp you've just got to  assume that your early PvP matches are  going to be a fight of fatigue you're  going to be trying to run out of blood  files after your opponent does rather  than overpowering them but hey that said  it's not impossible to overpower people  and maybe this will be a more valid  thing in the late game or maybe I'm just  not very good at the game my strategy in  PvP is to just stay as close as I can to  the opponent and shoot them whenever I  think they're going to be going for that  heal  usually I can chip them down until they  die or at least I can stun them so I can  get closer to them and continue my  assault and that's an interesting thing  too you can actually trigger a visceral  attack by timing your gun shot with  their heal they kneel down and then you  can go and start your post so once I get  good maybe this will be an option for me  or maybe in the late game weapons will  just do a lot more damage and it'll be  way easier to overpower people but as it  stands as you go through the game it's  very easy for them to heal oh and  speaking of visceral attacks you can  still initiate them the same way you  would in PvP when that enemy attacks you  and this is a really common thing it's  even better than parrying was in Dark  Souls because when you parried in Dark  Souls and you failed you still would  have got hit but if you shoot someone  and try to parry them in this game even  if you fail you still staggered them so  there's no real punishment if you fail  but while parrying and visceral attacks  is more popular I tell you what's not  more popular backstabs  you're not going to see many back stabs  in PvP I mean think about it you have to  fully charge are  and you have to hit them in the back so  unless they're afk that's not going to  happen off and I said this a thousand  times but the late-game pvp could look  completely different so if you're  subscribed I will make a video on that  when I feel confident in my beliefs  about it so look forward to that and  that's basically it that sums up my  thoughts I'm enjoying the PvP so much  I'm enjoying the game so much and I'm  really happy about the opportunity I  have to share it all with you guys ever  since I started on YouTube just playing  the game has never been enough all I  want to do is share my experience as  well and I want you guys to experience  that feeling as well which is actually a  bit of a hint for some upcoming videos  that I'm doing sharing your experiences  with me and the channel and with other  people is going to be a big thing so  really hope you look forward to that I'm  soaking to get it started but yeah  that'll come soon when I'm ready and  I'll talk to you guys later  thanks for watching  you
 

